o walk","H3644":"like","H4421":"battle","H1875":"to seek","H4994":"please","H3117":"day","H853":"[Obj.]","H1697":"word","H3068":"LORD","H6908":"to gather","H5030":"prophet","H702":"four","H3967":"hundred","H376":"man","H518":"if","H2308":"to cease","H5414":"give","H430":"God","H3027":"hand","H369":"nothing","H6311":"here","H5750":"still","H259":"one","H589":"I","H8130":"to hate","H3588":"for","H5012":"to prophesy","H5921":"upon","H2896":"pleasant","H3605":"all","H7451":"harmful","H1931":"he/she/it","H4321":"Micaiah","H1121":"child","H3229":"Imlah","H408":"not","H3651":"right","H7121":"call to","H5631":"eunuch","H4116":"to hasten","H4318":"Micah","H3427":"to dwell","H3678":"throne","H3847":"to clothe","H899":"treachery","H1637":"threshing floor","H6607":"entrance","H8179":"gate","H6440":"before","H6213":"do","H6667":"Zedekiah","H3668":"Chenaanah","H7161":"horn","H1270":"iron","H3541":"thus","H428":"these","H5055":"to gore","H758":"Aram","H5704":"till","H3615":"finish","H6743":"to rush","H4397":"messenger","H1980":"went","H1696":"speak","H2009":"behold","H6310":"lip","H2416":"alive","H935":"come","H4100":"what?","H6471":"beat","H7650":"to swear","H3808":"not","H7535":"except","H571":"faithful","H8034":"name","H7200":"see","H6327":"to scatter","H2022":"mount","H7462":"House of Shepherds","H113":"lord","H7725":"return","H1004":"place","H7965":"peace","H8085":"hear","H6635":"army","H8064":"heaven","H5975":"stand","H3225":"right","H8040":"left","H4310":"who?","H6601":"to open wide","H5307":"fall","H2088":"this","H3602":"thus","H3318":"come","H7307":"spirit","H8267":"deception","H1571":"also","H3201":"be able","H6258":"now","H5066":"approach","H5221":"to smite","H3895":"Lehi","H335":"where?","H1870":"conduct","H5674":"to pass","H854":"with","H2005":"look!","H2315":"chamber","H2244":"to hide","H3947":"take","H526":"Amon","H8269":"ruler","H5892":"excitement","H3101":"Joash","H7760":"make","H3608":"prison","H398":"to eat","H3899":"food","H3906":"oppression","H4325":"water","H2664":"to search","H859":"you(m.s.)","H6680":"to command","H7393":"chariot","H3898":"to fight","H6996":"small","H1419":"large","H905":"pole","H1992":"they(masc.)","H5437":"turn","H2199":"to cry out","H5826":"to help","H4480":"from","H310":"after","H4900":"to draw","H7198":"bow","H8537":"integrity","H996":"between","H1694":"joint","H8302":"lance","H7395":"charioteer","H2015":"to overturn","H4264":"camp","H2470":"weak","H4818":"chariot","H5227":"before","H6153":"evening","H4191":"to die","H6256":"time","H8121":"sun"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Affinity, taking Achab’s daughter for his son’s wife. (Tirinus) (Chap. xxi. 6., and 3 Kings xxii.)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","War. Josaphat was too complaisant. He was rebuked by the son of Hanani, as Asa had been by his father; (chap. xvi. 7.) and, not long after, Eliezer reproached him for joining in alliance with Ochozias, chap. xx. (Calmet) — He acted without an ill intention, and was more easily pardoned. (Worthington)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Hands. He ironically (Calmet) alludes to the declarations of the false prophets. (Haydock)"],["haydock",18,null,"haydock","Ye. In 3 Kings, he addresses his discourse chiefly to Achab. (Calmet)"],["haydock",20,null,"haydock","Said. See 3 Kings xxii. The Rabbins pretend that the spirit of Naboth came forth. But it was satan, or an evil spirit. (Tirinus)"],["haydock",21,null,"haydock","So. The Lord permits evil, but he does not approve of it. (Calmet) — Homer makes Jupiter send a deluding dream to Agamemnon. (Iliad B.) — The delusive predictions of impostors, are one great source of calamities. (Du Hamel)"],["haydock",25,null,"haydock","Amelech. Septuagint and Syriac, “to Joas, the commander, son of the father. (Haydock) — He had perhaps the government of affairs at Samaria, during his king.” Achab’s absence. (Tirinus)"],["haydock",27,null,"haydock","People. Mark what I say. The event will quickly prove whether I am a prophet or an impostor. (Haydock)"],["haydock",29,null,"haydock","Dress. Protestants, “disguised himself, and they went.” See 3 Kings xxii. 30."],["haydock",31,null,"haydock","Turned. Hebrew, “moved them from him.” They felt that he was under God’s protection; and discovered that he was not the king of Israel. (Haydock)"],["challoner",19,null,"challoner","Who shall deceive, etc.... See the annotations, 3 Kings 22."]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"],"challoner":["Richard Challoner",0,0,1781,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/03566a.htm"]},"fa":[[19,null,0,"Homilies on John","Homily 64",0,407,"For He also endured that many lowly things should be said concerning Him for the salvation of the hearers. ... In the case of Ahab it is said, \"Who shall entice Ahab for Me? And the continually preferring Himself to the gods of the heathen in the way of comparison, all these things are unworthy of God. Yet in another way they are made worthy of Him, for He is so kind, that for our salvation He careth not for expressions which become His dignity. …"]],"fau":[["chrysostom","John Chrysostom",1,"father",null,1,407]],"ftr":[["Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers, series 1, vol. 14 (1889)","https://ccel.org/ccel/schaff/npnf114"]]}